    "result": "Perfect! The fix is complete and verified. Here's a summary:\n\n## The Bug\n\nThe `frai gate init --ci` command wasn't creating the `.github/workflows/rai-gate.yml` file. The issue was that the `--ci` flag wasn't being passed through from the frai CLI to the frai-gate CLI.\n\n## The Root Cause\n\nIn `packages/frai-cli/src/index.ts`, the `gate` command handler was only using the `args` parameter:\n```typescript\nconst result = spawnSync(process.execPath, [gateCli, ...(args ?? [])], { stdio: 'inherit' });\n```\n\nWith `allowUnknownOption(true)`, Commander doesn't parse options like `--ci` into the option object. These unparsed options remain in `process.argv` but don't make it into the variadic `args` array.\n\n## The Fix\n\nI modified the handler to extract arguments directly from `process.argv`, starting after the 'gate' command name:\n\n```typescript\nconst gateIndex = process.argv.indexOf('gate');\nconst gateArgs = gateIndex >= 0 ? process.argv.slice(gateIndex + 1) : (args ?? []);\nconst result = spawnSync(process.execPath, [gateCli, ...gateArgs], { stdio: 'inherit' });\n```\n\nThis ensures all arguments\u2014including flags like `--ci`\u2014are properly forwarded to the frai-gate CLI.\n\n## Verification\n\nTested successfully:\n- \u2705 `FRAI-SPEC.md` is created\n- \u2705 `.github/workflows/rai-gate.yml` is now created with the `--ci` flag\n\nThe changes have been applied to both the source (`packages/frai-cli/src/index.ts`) and the compiled output (`packages/frai-cli/dist/index.js`).",
